From 4f2c5327d9fe788855fbc6ca9d688107fe144c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:54:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc/rc_ipsec: bound profile field parsing + IP copies (H6/M2)

H6: ipsec_profile_str_parse() copied each '>'-delimited token from the
nvram ipsec_profile_N string into fixed struct fields (virtual_subnet[32],
local_id[128], auth_method_key[33], ...) with no bound, and then
strcat(".0/24") could push virtual_subnet past its end. Add a destination
size parameter that bounds the write while still advancing the source
pointer (so token-shift accounting is unchanged), update all 26 call
sites to pass sizeof(field), and convert the ".0/24" append to a bounded
snprintf.

M2: replace the unbounded strcpy() of wan0/wan1/lan _ipaddr nvram into
left_ipaddr[16] (3 sites) and into prof[].local_pub_ip (4 sites) with
snprintf bounded by sizeof(dest).

Compiles clean with the real userspace toolchain; warn-diff vs the
pre-hardening baseline shows zero new warning categories.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/rc_ipsec.c | 88 +++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/rc_ipsec.c b/release/src/router/rc/rc_ipsec.c
index a76d346733..d1ac79cf47 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/rc_ipsec.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/rc_ipsec.c
